%% The same data through three lenses. Scores are satisfaction, 1 to 5, for the
%% person in that row - they show where the design intends to remove friction.
journey
  title One day in a sprint, by role
  section Team member
    Open My work, see what is asked of me: 4: Member
    Type or dictate one update: 5: Member
    Let the agent tidy it, then confirm: 5: Member
    Answer "are you blocked?" honestly: 4: Member
    Get a runbook and a name to ask: 5: Member
  section Facilitator
    Open Overview, read the roll-up banner: 5: Facilitator
    Triage ranked signals with evidence: 5: Facilitator
    Approve or edit a proposed change: 4: Facilitator
    See who has gone quiet, not who is slow: 4: Facilitator
    Close the sprint with a retro that cites causes: 5: Facilitator
  section Manager
    Open the aggregate overview: 4: Manager
    See delivery risk, not individuals: 5: Manager
    Read adoption - accepted vs dismissed: 4: Manager
